      'Rule example: Score points: High (1), Low (1), Jack (1), Game (1). Total 4 points per hand (or more in variants with Joker).',
      'Turn-flow example: Six cards each. One round of bidding (2 to 4); high bidder names trump and leads. Follow suit; may trump when void (in some variants may trump while holding led suit). Four points per hand: High (ace of trump), Low (deuce of trump), Jack (trick with jack of trumps), Game (side with more card points in tricks: A=4 K=3 Q=2 J=1 10=10). First team to reach target (e.g. 15 or 21) wins.',
      "Scoring example: High (highest trump in play), Low (lowest trump in playâ€”goes to holder or winner? In Pitch, usually to holder. In Smear, usually to winner of trick? Check rules: In 'Smear', Low often goes to the *capturer* of the low trump, making it distinct from Pitch where it goes to the original holder. Four points per hand: High (player who plays ace of trump), Low (player who plays deuce of trump), Jack (side that wins trick containing jack of trumps), Game (side with more card points in tricks: A=4 K=3 Q=2 J=1 10=10). If bidding side makes at least their bid they score what they made; otherwise they lose the bid amount. First team to reach target (e.g. 15 or 21) wins. Score points: High (1), Low (1), Jack (1), Game (1). Total 4 points per hand (or more in variants with Joker). First team to reach agreed target score wins..",
